--TEST--
A placeholder the data does not have throws a `LogicError` naming it and its cell, for a value and for an item of a list, and a list inside an item throws naming both lists: rule:core-classes/spreadsheet-template-fill
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Novis\Spreadsheet\Template::open
// covers: Novis\Spreadsheet\Template::fill
// covers: Novis\Spreadsheet\Export::bytes
use Novis\Spreadsheet\Template;
use Novis\Spreadsheet\Workbook;

// This workbook is the template. Row 2 is the item row.
var $design = Workbook::createInMemory();
$design->sheet("Invoice")->addAll([
    ["Invoice {{number}}", "{{customer.name}}"],
    ["{{items.name}}", "{{items.qty}}"],
]);
bytes $template = $design->finish()->bytes ?? Core\Bytes::fill(0, 0);

// The data has no `customer`, so `fill` throws an error.
try {
    Template::open($template)->fill(["number" => 42, "items" => []]);
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}

// The second item has no `qty`. The items are written by `bytes`, so `bytes` throws the error.
try {
    Template::open($template)->fill([
        "number" => 42,
        "customer" => ["name" => "Shop"],
        "items" => [["name" => "Pen", "qty" => 2], ["name" => "Ink"]],
    ])->bytes();
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}

// An item cannot have a list of its own.
try {
    Template::open($template)->fill([
        "number" => 42,
        "customer" => ["name" => "Shop"],
        "items" => [["name" => "Pen", "qty" => 2, "colors" => ["red", "blue"]]],
    ])->bytes();
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
The template's cell `Invoice!B1` has the placeholder `{{customer.name}}`, which the data does not have.
The template's cell `Invoice!B2` has the placeholder `{{items.qty}}`, which the data does not have.
The list `colors` is inside the list `items`. A template cannot repeat a list inside a list.
